To set the number of probes for a single query only, use `SET LOCAL` inside a transaction:

```sql
BEGIN;
SET LOCAL ivfflat.probes = 10;
SELECT ...
COMMIT;
```

[chunk 307]

The documentation recommends enabling relaxed-order iterative scans (for better recall) combined with a materialized CTE to re-impose strict ordering afterward:

```sql
SET hnsw.iterative_scan = relaxed_order;
# or
SET ivfflat.iterative_scan = relaxed_order;
```

```sql
WITH relaxed_results AS MATERIALIZED (
    SELECT id, embedding <-> '[1,2,3]' AS distance FROM items WHERE category_id = 123 ORDER BY distance LIMIT 5
) SELECT * FROM relaxed_results ORDER BY distance + 0;
```

Note: `+ 0` is needed for Postgres 17+ [chunk 313]

This works because "Relaxed allows results to be slightly out of order by distance, but provides better recall," and "With relaxed ordering, you can use a materialized CTE ... to get strict ordering." [chunk 313]
